---
description: Use for Frick MCP runtime setup, live app inspection, agent tool/resource/prompt integration, and MCP safety boundaries.
alwaysApply: false
---

Use `frick mcp` as the standard entrypoint for connecting agents to a running Frick app. Default MCP mode is read-only.

Expose documented Frick runtime surfaces: health, readiness, schema identity, inspection, stream pages, jobs, dashboard-compatible diagnostics, and structured error explanation.

Do not expose raw SQL, private storage internals, or tenant-crossing reads. Mutating MCP tools require explicit `--allow-writes` and must preserve Frick auth, tenant isolation, schema compatibility, and structured error envelopes.
